<!-- awf:section working-memory -->
## Working memory

Discovery creates no effort. Before first creation for a concrete non-minimal outcome, present the labeled outcome, proposed effort title, and proposed short effort slug, ask the user to confirm creation, and end the turn without mutation; only a clear response in a later turn confirming all three fields permits `awf effort new --slug <confirmed-slug> "<confirmed-title>"`. A minimal simple fix uses no effort. An existing effort resumes under its fixed identity without title reconfirmation only for work inside its confirmed outcome; a newly discovered outcome cannot silently reuse, rename, replace, or create beside that active effort. A confirmed outcome uses exactly one immutable slugged effort, which always owns `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md`. The effort's managed worktree is the default execution location (`--no-worktree` is the explicit exception), while the owned memory stays under the primary checkout. Carry the slug and exact path through mandatory checkpoints, but verify checkpoint claims against repository sources and current-state documentation.{{if .targetSessionHandoff}} A routine checkpoint persists the effort and then permits a discretionary eligible session-replacement choice; a safe resumable point has an immediate successor that can start independently. The new session logs an actual replacement boundary as its first memory update before substantive work, while in-session continuation or a replacement that leaves the old session active logs none.{{end}} Mandatory first-creation confirmation stops before effort allocation; final brainstorming and ADR approval remain explicit stops until their approval and next action are persisted. One effort has one user-managed writer; report-only children and helpers never edit shared memory. Never create standalone memory, commit the owned file, or cite its concrete path in an ADR, plan, or commit message. Worktree-backed efforts integrate and remove topology after terminal review and before retrospective; retrospective finishes the effort last. The detailed protocol lives in the workflow doc's working-memory section.
<!-- awf:end -->

